that are normal, or that are subims (trivial subgroups), they are actually all
congruent to each other. -/
theorem conjugate_of_mem {a : G | ∃ h, h ∈ H ∧ a = x * h * x⁻¹} {G' : Type*} [Group G'] where
  id := by simp only [Homomorph.id, GroupHomomorph, Subid, Subgroup.id, mul_comm]
  map_to := by simp only [Subgroup.map_to, id_apply, mul_comm]
  mem_car := fun hₗ hₗ' ↦ by simp [id_apply, mul_comm, hₗ, hₗ']
